        "id": "ch10_2-1",
        "text": "Planning for disaster recovery\nManaging risks is an important asset for every business or individual. The responsibility of this is\ntremendous for everyone involved in system administration. For all businesses, managing risks should\nbe part of a wider risk management strategy . There are various types of risks in IT, starting from\nnatural hazards directly impacting data centers or business locations, all the way up to cyber security\nthreats. IT\u2019s footprint inside a company has exponentially grown in the last decade. Nowadays, there\nis no activity that does not involve some sort of IT operations being behind it, be it inside small\nbusinesses, big corporations, government agencies, or the health and education public sectors, just to\ngive a few examples. Each activity is unique in its own way, so it needs a specific type of assessment.\nUnfortunately, with regard to the information security field, risk management has largely evolved into\na one-size-fits-all practice, based on checklists that should be implemented by IT management. Let\u2019s\nbegin with a brief introduction to risk management before moving on to learning how we can assess risk.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 A brief introduction to risk management\n\u2022 Risk calculation\n\u2022 Designing a DRP\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
